      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Statutory RTO Paperwork, Transit Marine Insurance &amp; Delivery Handover for Transport from Pondicherry Hyderabad</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;">
	<p>When transporting your car from Pondicherry to Hyderabad, it is essential to provide the following documents to ensure a smooth and hassle-free experience.</p>

	<p>The Road Transport Corporation (RTC) registration certificate (RC) is a crucial document that confirms the ownership of the vehicle. It serves as proof of your legal rights to transport the car. To ensure the process is hassle-free, ensure that the RC copy is self-attested.</p>

	<p>The Pollution Under Control (PUC) certificate confirms that the vehicle meets environmental standards and is in good working condition. A valid PUC should be provided, indicating that the car has been checked within the last 30 days.</p>

	<p>It is mandatory to have a valid insurance certificate for your car during transport. This document covers any potential damages or accidents that may occur during the transportation process. Ensure that the insurance certificate is valid and covers the entire transportation period.</p>

	<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">The Indian Bureau of Mines (IBA) approved consignment bill of lading is a document that serves as a contract between the car owner and the transport company.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>It outlines the details of the car, transportation method, insurance coverage, and pickup and delivery locations.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>Ensure that the bill of lading is IBA-approved to avoid any inconvenience during the transportation process.</span></li></ul>

	<p>To ensure the car is adequately insured during transport, it is essential to provide a declared value document. This document indicates the declared value of your car, which will be used to calculate the insurance coverage during transit.</p>

	<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">To provide additional protection for your car during transportation, it is recommended to opt for a 100% declared value marine transit insurance.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>This insurance covers the car against any damages or accidents that may occur during sea transportation.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>By opting for this coverage, you can have peace of mind knowing that your car is fully insured throughout the journey.</span></li></ul>

	<p>The VIN (Vehicle Identification Number) is a unique code assigned to your car by the manufacturer. It is essential to provide the vehicle's VIN number during the transportation process. Additionally, it is recommended to provide the registration details, including the vehicle registration number and owner's name.</p>

	<p>To ensure a smooth transportation process, you will need to fill out and sign declaration and authorization forms provided by the transport company. These forms authorize the company to transport your car, as well as provide important details about the car, such as make, model, year, and mileage.</p>
